From 6a8c222af477034b8434f8e2351d29ad6ab40a77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:07:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(byoc): batch events + Python worker

Send claude stream-json events to the server in batches (action: "events")
instead of one synchronous POST per line. The POSIX worker buffers up to 50
events and flushes every ~150ms or on queue pressure, dropping the oldest
event under severe congestion so claude's stdout never stalls. Falls back to
single-event POSTs against an older server. The worker now also exits
promptly when the node token is revoked (HTTP 401) and terminates the active
claude child on SIGTERM/SIGINT instead of orphaning it.

Server route adds a bounded batch endpoint (non-empty, <=100 events per call)
that publishes each event and reports the accepted count; it rejects with 409
and the accepted-so-far count when a run is not running or an event is invalid.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
